WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.310
Why do we launch rockets in Florida?

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:06.840
I remember&nbsp;as a kid just not getting it as I watched these rocket launches get scrubbed

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.556
due to bad weather.

00:00:08.556 --> 00:00:11.160
I was like, you guys know that's Florida right?

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.654
that's where they get the hurricanes and the&nbsp;
thunderstorms .

00:00:13.654 --> 00:00:18.564
and you know one of the Apollo missions got hit by a lightning strike on its way&nbsp;out of the atmosphere

00:00:18.564 --> 00:00:19.684
it's unbelievable

00:00:19.684 --> 00:00:23.669
but there are two very good reasons why they launch rockets from here.

00:00:23.669 --> 00:00:29.271
the first is because the ground beneath our feet is moving to the East very&nbsp;fast

00:00:29.271 --> 00:00:32.929
Everything is going about 900 miles per hour

00:00:32.929 --> 00:00:35.966
that's 1500 kilometers per hour

00:00:35.966 --> 00:00:39.412
and that means as&nbsp;
your rocket takes off up and to the east

00:00:39.412 --> 00:00:42.085
it starts off with that velocity.

00:00:42.085 --> 00:00:45.472
The Earth is giving that&nbsp;
rocket an initial boost so you don't have to put

00:00:45.472 --> 00:00:47.499
in as much energy. You don't have to speed it up as&nbsp;much.

00:00:47.499 --> 00:00:52.425
Now the other thing is if you're gonna fly to the East and something goes wrong with that rocket

00:00:52.425 --> 00:00:54.901
you're going to want it to not hurt anything

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.974
what's nice about Florida is what you have over&nbsp;there is ocean

00:00:57.974 --> 00:00:59.559
not the rest of your country.

